(78596, 2777, 2478, '<td valign="top">Very cool concept. Some light bounced off the ceiling would make the background stand out more. Or, since main light source seems to be coming from the right, did you try orienting the objects so that they received full frontal lighting? They''re a bit subdued without more light.<br/>Hmmm. Lighten the foreground objects, or lighten the background? I can''t decide. Either way, this is a great composition.</td>', 'Very cool concept. Some light bounced off the ceiling would make the background stand out more. Or, since main light source seems to be coming from the right, did you try orienting the objects so that they received full frontal lighting? They''re a bit subdued without more light.Hmmm. Lighten the foreground objects, or lighten the background? I can''t decide. Either way, this is a great composition.', '2002-07-04 01:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78597, 2777, 509, '<td valign="top">Intersting shot, but i think it needs more lighting (not flash).  More lighting in the room would help the colors I think, but some subtle lighting under the table might make it even better.  Also, I don''t know if it would help, but a polarizer might get rid of the glare on the bowl.  Good interpretation of transparency!</td>', 'Intersting shot, but i think it needs more lighting (not flash).  More lighting in the room would help the colors I think, but some subtle lighting under the table might make it even better.  Also, I don''t know if it would help, but a polarizer might get rid of the glare on the bowl.  Good interpretation of transparency!', '2002-07-05 16:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
