(78852, 2803, 806, '<td valign="top">Another one I am in awe over! Very cool. Again... my guess: long exposure, run in, pose, run to next position, pose, run out? How does this happen without blur lines? Maybe you can get together with the other photographer who did something similar for a how to?</td>', 'Another one I am in awe over! Very cool. Again... my guess: long exposure, run in, pose, run to next position, pose, run out? How does this happen without blur lines? Maybe you can get together with the other photographer who did something similar for a how to?', '2002-07-01 18:28:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(78853, 2803, 693, '<td valign="top">Excellent creativity!  This is very odd... the shadows cast by the two individuals point towards the light source in the sky as opposed to away.  Which leads me to believe the light source is coming from a similar location as where the camera is. I''m racking my brain trying to figure this one out. I''d like to know how you did this, please explain once the challenge is over.  9.  Brumos</td>', 'Excellent creativity!  This is very odd... the shadows cast by the two individuals point towards the light source in the sky as opposed to away.  Which leads me to believe the light source is coming from a similar location as where the camera is. I''m racking my brain trying to figure this one out. I''d like to know how you did this, please explain once the challenge is over.  9.  Brumos', '2002-07-01 18:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
