(79787, 2870, 472, '<td valign="top">i like to take the offbeat path, so i steered away from glass and water.  i had taken a macro of my cat''s eye before that came out really nice, so i wanted to try it again.  the cat''s eye really has a lot more curvature than the human''s.  <br/><br/>well, kitty wasn''t so cooperative this time, she kept trying to nuzzle the camera and roll over. so i turned to my long-suffering wife : ) ..  i tried a number of angles and came up with this amazing edge lighting that really seemed to evoke someone looking at the something visionary.  <br/><br/>the light source is a bare bulb about 5 feet away in front of the eye and a little bit to her right hand side.<br/><br/>this was a fun one.  thanks for all the positiivity, folks : )</td>', 'i like to take the offbeat path, so i steered away from glass and water.  i had taken a macro of my cat''s eye before that came out really nice, so i wanted to try it again.  the cat''s eye really has a lot more curvature than the human''s.  well, kitty wasn''t so cooperative this time, she kept trying to nuzzle the camera and roll over. so i turned to my long-suffering wife : ) ..  i tried a number of angles and came up with this amazing edge lighting that really seemed to evoke someone looking at the something visionary.  the light source is a bare bulb about 5 feet away in front of the eye and a little bit to her right hand side.this was a fun one.  thanks for all the positiivity, folks : )', '2002-07-08 14:32:00.000000', NULL, 0),
