(80131, 2892, 2154, '<td valign="top">I would like to know how this was accomplished.  Would it be out of line for the photographer to e-mail me?   macaron002@aol.com</td>', 'I would like to know how this was accomplished.  Would it be out of line for the photographer to e-mail me?   macaron002@aol.com', '2002-07-06 16:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(80132, 2892, 1031, '<td valign="top">I love the illusion of depth you get with this technique. I''m not a huge fan of using the flag motif, but it works well here. Isaac just walked by and said "cool, American footballs!"</td>', 'I love the illusion of depth you get with this technique. I''m not a huge fan of using the flag motif, but it works well here. Isaac just walked by and said "cool, American footballs!"', '2002-07-06 19:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(80133, 2892, 1128, '<td valign="top">Wooooooow!  Wish I''d had THIS idea.<br/>Oh wait, I did!    :)       (flowerdrops)<br/>This is a spectacular capture!  Clear, crisp and just wonderful colors.  Can''t wait to swap stories about how you did it.</td>', 'Wooooooow!  Wish I''d had THIS idea.Oh wait, I did!    :)       (flowerdrops)This is a spectacular capture!  Clear, crisp and just wonderful colors.  Can''t wait to swap stories about how you did it.', '2002-07-07 10:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(80134, 2892, 2235, '<td valign="top">Depth of field works well with this shot. Overall size of water drops provides even distribution of the flag in its multiple versions across the frame. Very colorfull and well done.</td>', 'Depth of field works well with this shot. Overall size of water drops provides even distribution of the flag in its multiple versions across the frame. Very colorfull and well done.', '2002-07-07 11:38:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(80135, 2892, 2, '<td valign="top">Yes, we all know you''re gonna win -- nicely done, John :)  My only complaint is that the lighting seems uneven.  That is, the white of the background flag at the bottom left seems darker than that at the top right.  Could be my eyes..</td>', 'Yes, we all know you''re gonna win -- nicely done, John :)  My only complaint is that the lighting seems uneven.  That is, the white of the background flag at the bottom left seems darker than that at the top right.  Could be my eyes..', '2002-07-08 00:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(80136, 2892, 772, '<td valign="top">I would like to thank everyone for the great comments on this photo.  Im not going to go into details about it here because I have prepared a Howd They Do That for the site.  The only brief comments that I wish to make are:  1) I wish I had known about the Popular Photography photo before I did this.  I would have used my other idea instead, which is shown in my Howd They Do That article.  2) The Popular Photography photo was NOT my inspiration for this shot.  The photos that inspired this shot are listed in my article as well.  My objective was to produce a BETTER image than the ones I listed.  3) I dont believe that duplicating ideas that others have already done is wrong in any way.  If this was the case, every photographer who photographs the Eiffel Tower or the White House would have to give credit to the first person who did it, right? J  <br/><br/>I spend too much time looking at photography online.  Because of this, I see quite a few photos that are duplicated ideas.  I dont hold that against the photographer.  Cheers to all, and I hope everyone who celebrated Independence Day in the US had a safe and happy weekend J<br/></td>', 'I would like to thank everyone for the great comments on this photo.  Im not going to go into details about it here because I have prepared a Howd They Do That for the site.  The only brief comments that I wish to make are:  1) I wish I had known about the Popular Photography photo before I did this.  I would have used my other idea instead, which is shown in my Howd They Do That article.  2) The Popular Photography photo was NOT my inspiration for this shot.  The photos that inspired this shot are listed in my article as well.  My objective was to produce a BETTER image than the ones I listed.  3) I dont believe that duplicating ideas that others have already done is wrong in any way.  If this was the case, every photographer who photographs the Eiffel Tower or the White House would have to give credit to the first person who did it, right? J  I spend too much time looking at photography online.  Because of this, I see quite a few photos that are duplicated ideas.  I dont hold that against the photographer.  Cheers to all, and I hope everyone who celebrated Independence Day in the US had a safe and happy weekend J', '2002-07-08 01:19:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(80137, 2892, 92, '<td valign="top">You go boy !!!!! You earned this one !!!!!!!!</td>', 'You go boy !!!!! You earned this one !!!!!!!!', '2002-07-08 01:21:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(80138, 2892, 1897, '<td valign="top"><br/>great job john (alka), and great high score!.  So much for that hole "scores are getting lower" thread. One of my few favorites that did well.  Seven 1''s is just wrong.  Great job man, I am seriously jealous, or is it envious?  Envious.</td>', 'great job john (alka), and great high score!.  So much for that hole "scores are getting lower" thread. One of my few favorites that did well.  Seven 1''s is just wrong.  Great job man, I am seriously jealous, or is it envious?  Envious.', '2002-07-08 01:27:00.000000', NULL, 0),
