(80520, 2921, 1005, '<td valign="top">ewww, math....well depicted shot.  O.K. I just realized the pen is blue, how did you get the rest to look sooo black and white?  Photo 7 Transparency 6 total 7 swash</td>', 'ewww, math....well depicted shot.  O.K. I just realized the pen is blue, how did you get the rest to look sooo black and white?  Photo 7 Transparency 6 total 7 swash', '2002-07-02 16:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(80521, 2921, 1379, '<td valign="top">Aaaaah, math.  I love this.</td>', 'Aaaaah, math.  I love this.', '2002-07-02 23:24:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(80522, 2921, 1856, '<td valign="top">I really like this image.  Funny how it looks desaturated until you notice the blue pen.  To me the emphasis is more on the girl in the background and not the transparency so it looses a point there.  Great job!</td>', 'I really like this image.  Funny how it looks desaturated until you notice the blue pen.  To me the emphasis is more on the girl in the background and not the transparency so it looses a point there.  Great job!', '2002-07-03 10:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(80523, 2921, 637, '<td valign="top">It is technically pleasing and it meets the challenge, but only peripherally.  The main subject (for me) is the sleepy student, not the magnified formulae seen through the specs.  5 sjgleah</td>', 'It is technically pleasing and it meets the challenge, but only peripherally.  The main subject (for me) is the sleepy student, not the magnified formulae seen through the specs.  5 sjgleah', '2002-07-03 11:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(80524, 2921, 772, '<td valign="top">I have been here before :) great shot.. I think the only thing that is keeping me from giving this photo a 10 is the lighting.  The amount of light is perfect but I think a little more contrast may be in order possibly.  I would love to see the skin tones contrasting a little more with the paper, but that''s probably impossible... good shot! = 9 - jmsetzler</td>', 'I have been here before :) great shot.. I think the only thing that is keeping me from giving this photo a 10 is the lighting.  The amount of light is perfect but I think a little more contrast may be in order possibly.  I would love to see the skin tones contrasting a little more with the paper, but that''s probably impossible... good shot! = 9 - jmsetzler', '2002-07-06 01:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(80525, 2921, 1054, '<td valign="top">Well-executed.  I like this shot.</td>', 'Well-executed.  I like this shot.', '2002-07-07 11:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(80526, 2921, 1041, '<td valign="top">my top 10 this week -- gr8photos (9)</td>', 'my top 10 this week -- gr8photos (9)', '2002-07-08 01:02:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(80527, 2921, 1041, '<td valign="top">sorry, i ran out of time to comment.  i was going to say that i really like the blue pens against the b&amp;w of the rest of the photo.  how did you do that?</td>', 'sorry, i ran out of time to comment.  i was going to say that i really like the blue pens against the b&w of the rest of the photo.  how did you do that?', '2002-07-08 11:05:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(80528, 2921, 2004, '<td valign="top">To get the "blue pen", I augmented contrast and luminosity, and then desaturated red, yellow and green with the "Image--Adjust--Hue/Saturation" option in Photoshop. I agree that the challenge topic is not really well empasized here, but I''m happy with the result. Thanks for all your votes and comments.</td>', 'To get the "blue pen", I augmented contrast and luminosity, and then desaturated red, yellow and green with the "Image--Adjust--Hue/Saturation" option in Photoshop. I agree that the challenge topic is not really well empasized here, but I''m happy with the result. Thanks for all your votes and comments.', '2002-07-08 12:28:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(80529, 2922, 1, '<td valign="top">Not seeing too much transparency here, but the effect is cool.</td>', 'Not seeing too much transparency here, but the effect is cool.', '2002-07-01 09:35:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(80530, 2922, 436, '<td valign="top">great title, fun effect!</td>', 'great title, fun effect!', '2002-07-01 11:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
