(80872, 2958, 737, '<td valign="top">Great abstract</td>', 'Great abstract', '2002-07-07 23:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(80873, 2958, 2172, '<td valign="top">I am very excited about this photo.  THANKS TO ALL!!!   I appreciate all of the comments.<br/>Brief notes about the photo:<br/>    Plastic covers to small containers<br/>    Clear Candle Gel Wax - dyed to the primary colors - red, blue, yellow<br/>    At first, my objective was to display the creation of additional colors with the primary colors through transparency using gel wax and light. - This took three separate days because of my lack of knowledge of using the white-balance of my camera.  Many of the first photos came out very yellow and/or greyish instead of white.  On the third try, I used another (new to me) setting for the white balance and learned how to use it.<br/>    Setting up sturdyboard and two living-room floor lamps (less the shades) and the sticky gel wax was fun and at the same time frustrating - my cats knocked over the sturdyboard onto the plastic covers and the wax stuck to the boards - I should''ve taken a photo of my setup for the Bloopers page!  <br/>    The final photo was obtained through a little cropping - Thank you very much to those who helped out in the Cropping thread, it really really made a difference for me - and a small global hue adjustment, a touch of contrast and gamma adjustment.  The only reason I changed the hue was because the original colors didn''t seem to stand out as much.<br/>    I had a very hard time choosing which one to enter - I had to have a couple of friends and family members pick it out, then we had to name it.  moppenheimer commented:  pitry dish explosion - I like that one.<br/><br/>Thank you again!   I''ve been enjoying this site very much and have learned a great deal from the people here!!<br/><br/>Congrats to the winners this week and to everyone for a job well done!!!!<br/><br/>Ruthann</td>', 'I am very excited about this photo.  THANKS TO ALL!!!   I appreciate all of the comments.Brief notes about the photo:    Plastic covers to small containers    Clear Candle Gel Wax - dyed to the primary colors - red, blue, yellow    At first, my objective was to display the creation of additional colors with the primary colors through transparency using gel wax and light. - This took three separate days because of my lack of knowledge of using the white-balance of my camera.  Many of the first photos came out very yellow and/or greyish instead of white.  On the third try, I used another (new to me) setting for the white balance and learned how to use it.    Setting up sturdyboard and two living-room floor lamps (less the shades) and the sticky gel wax was fun and at the same time frustrating - my cats knocked over the sturdyboard onto the plastic covers and the wax stuck to the boards - I should''ve taken a photo of my setup for the Bloopers page!      The final photo was obtained through a little cropping - Thank you very much to those who helped out in the Cropping thread, it really really made a difference for me - and a small global hue adjustment, a touch of contrast and gamma adjustment.  The only reason I changed the hue was because the original colors didn''t seem to stand out as much.    I had a very hard time choosing which one to enter - I had to have a couple of friends and family members pick it out, then we had to name it.  moppenheimer commented:  pitry dish explosion - I like that one.Thank you again!   I''ve been enjoying this site very much and have learned a great deal from the people here!!Congrats to the winners this week and to everyone for a job well done!!!!Ruthann', '2002-07-08 12:15:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(80874, 2959, 772, '<td valign="top">Not bad :) I think I expected to see this shot but you did it rather well :) = 6 - jmsetzler</td>', 'Not bad :) I think I expected to see this shot but you did it rather well :) = 6 - jmsetzler', '2002-07-01 08:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
